s-west, eu-west), with an 18% error rate. The pre-release v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging. We rolled back all regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. After the rollback, all regions run v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is 0.2%. Next steps: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression before redeploying it.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 52239, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01ELmaQxWQaczuWkqoUYEypF", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconciled_executed", "postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 52239, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01ELmaQxWQaczuWkqoUYEypF", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 55411, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened a SEV2 incident.\n\n- **Problem:** The latest release, v2.3.1, was failing health checks in all three regions (us-east, us-west and eu-west), with an 18% error rate. Its test version (v2.3.1-rc) had also failed health checks in staging.\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. All three regions now run it, and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 (SEV2) describes the failure and the rollback, and lists finding the cause before v2.3.1 is deployed again as the next step. Opening it paged the on-call engineer.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01UVVoNYVEJx7VqTPwfSL5ik", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "ch